menu "ProtoScope local UI (OLED display and rotary encoder)"

    config PROTO_UI_AUTOSTART
        bool "Start the UI task, OLED display and encoder at boot"
        default y
        help
            The display (GPIO14 SDA, GPIO10 SCL) and encoder (GPIO1, GPIO2, GPIO6) pins stay
            parked until the UI starts. Turn this off for console-only operation.

    config PROTO_DISPLAY_OLED_FLIP
        bool "Rotate the OLED picture 180 degrees"
        default n
        help
            Use this if your module is mounted upside down. It can also be changed live
            with the console command 'display flip on|off'.

    config PROTO_ENCODER_STEPS_PER_DETENT
        int "Signal changes per encoder click (1..4)"
        range 1 4
        default 4
        help
            Most 20-click EC11/KY-040 knobs produce 4 changes per click (use 4). Knobs with
            30 clicks per turn produce 2 (use 2). If one click moves the menu by two lines,
            use 4; if you have to turn two clicks to move one line, use 2. Can also be
            changed live with 'ui encoder steps N'.

    config PROTO_ENCODER_INVERT
        bool "Reverse the encoder direction"
        default n
        help
            Can also be changed live with 'ui invert on|off'.
endmenu
